────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. GUIDE CONTENT  —  CC BY-SA 4.0
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Applies to: the written walkthroughs themselves — the prose, checklists,
tables, diagrams and research notes in `games/*/stages/`,
`games/*/reference/`, `games/*/index.html`, and `docs/verified-facts/`.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
License (CC BY-SA 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

In short: you may share and adapt this material, including commercially, as
long as you give appropriate credit and license your derivative work under the
same terms. Translating a guide into another language, or building on the
research in `docs/verified-facts/`, is exactly the kind of reuse this licence
is chosen to allow.

Why share-alike for the content: the value here is the verification work — every
fact carries two independent sources and a date. ShareAlike keeps corrections
and translations flowing back into the commons rather than being enclosed.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. WHAT IS NOT COVERED
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Neither licence grants any right in the games being described.

Game titles, character names, place names, item names, mechanics and all other
elements of the games remain the property of their respective owners. They are
referred to here descriptively, to identify the things a player sees on screen,
which is the only way a walkthrough can function.

This project is **unofficial and unaffiliated**. It is not endorsed by,
sponsored by, or connected with any game publisher or developer.

No game assets are redistributed here — no screenshots, sprites, audio,
textures or extracted data. Every diagram is drawn from scratch as inline SVG,
and every page is original writing.

If you are a rights holder and believe something in this repository oversteps,
open an issue and it will be addressed.
